//api.github.com/users/Calinou/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"Tested locally, it works as expected. Code looks good to me.\n\nThis makes sense from an usability standpoint, but also from a performance standpoint as snapping to collision data is potentially much faster when using simplified collision data. This would be one more reason to merge https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/82649, so that more imported 3D scenes use simplified collision data 🙂 \n\nNote that CSG's **Use Collision** property is not considered as collision, since the collision shape does not have a visual representation in the editor. I think it should act like it does at runtime to better match user expectations. This can likely be achieved by treating CSG mesh visual data as collision if the **Use Collision** property is enabled, making it snappable to even when **Snap to Collision Vertices** is used.","state":"COMMENTED","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/117887#pullrequestreview-4077723810","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/117887","author_association":"MEMBER","_links":{"html":{"href":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/117887#pullrequestreview-4077723810"},"pull_request":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/117887"}},"submitted_at":"2026-04-08T19:28:38Z","commit_id":null},{"id":4108308872,"node_id":"PRR_kwDOAO6SJc7039GI","user":{"login":"Calinou","id":180032,"node